TI  - Understanding spatiotemporal clustering of seasonal influenza in the United States
JO  - BMC Infectious Diseases
AB  - Seasonal influenza exhibits distinct spatiotemporal patterns across the United States, yet the geographic clustering of influenza activity remains incompletely understood. This study aims to identify jurisdictions with similar patterns of seasonal influenza epidemics by exploring spatiotemporal dynamics across the United States after the 2009 H1N1 pandemic.
